[quote="TakeWalker"]

So&nbsp;<em>that&#39;s</em> what Overhaul Loadout is for! I&#39;ve just been using it as go-to from-hand discard fodder. :B Then again, my playstyle with him is still &quot;just play whatever and stuff happens&quot;. The best strategy I can do is getting the start-of-turn power use and using it to boost his damage for the turn. That always feels good. :DGlad to see these guides are still a thing!

[/quote]

i wanted to get that point across better than I did. But your style of &ldquo;just play stuff and see what happens&rdquo; isn&rsquo;t just your play style for his deck, that&rsquo;s the play style of the deck.

You don&rsquo;t usually get an option for which hardware you look for first, let&rsquo;s say in the same way the Argent or Wraith have ways to decide their lines of play. Benchmark is at the whim of the deck, and depending on which hardware you pull first can really dictate to a large degree where you&rsquo;re next synergies and card plays should be focused. Finding LegionCore first is very different from finding Coolant to finding Fabricator.&nbsp;

The difference in playing his deck and playing his deck well is knowing exactly how the bigger picture is supposed to fit together so you can make the best lines of play when you&rsquo;re just starting the setup.&nbsp;

&nbsp;

Also so if you play mostly on mobile, Overhauls re-organization ability is easy to miss, but when you&rsquo;re actually playing him physically it&rsquo;s a small godsend.&nbsp;

